## --- Status correction (append-only: last occurrence wins) ---

ex:Lineage4 backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_InProgress ;
    rdfs:comment "Chain closed (Mission through Backlog, one stage per commit); the Backlog stage's StageOutput moves the lineage to LS_InProgress, same point at which Lineage3 made the same move."@en .

ex:Lineage4 backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Achieved ;
    rdfs:comment "9/9 Backlog4 items Done (ST4_StateCheck, ST4_DraftCh11, ST4_DraftCh12, ST4_ApprovalGate, ST4_RenderCh11, ST4_RenderCh12, ST4_YaRetirement, and the two state-check tasks they decompose into); closure report written and the owner's confirmation of LS_Achieved given 2026-11-10. backlog_lineage_archive scheduled for the next release per G215, not run in this version."@en .

ex:Mission4 backlog:hasMissionOutcome "Chapters 11 and 12 of the third edition are each taught from one owner-approved draft, with their decks and pages already matching that draft verbatim and no open item remaining." ;
    backlog:outcomeRationale "Both chapters' state checks found no gap against the current story and resources-slide standard, so the drafts were a direct write-up rather than a correction pass; the owner approved both without change; the render check found the existing deck and page already carried the approved content, so no new version was declared; and the one real finding outside the mission's own checks - the legacy Chapter9OrganizingFiles_YA_v1_0_0.pptx duplicating chapter 11's subject - was raised, decided by the owner, and closed within this same lineage, leaving nothing carried forward." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
